  "Question": "Calculate: \\(6 \\div (\\frac{2}{5}) = ?\\)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "15",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Dividing by the nonzero fraction \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) means multiplying by its reciprocal, \\(\\frac{5}{2}\\). Therefore\n\\[\n6 \\div \\frac{2}{5} = 6 \\times \\frac{5}{2} = \\frac{30}{2} = 15.\n\\]",
